### Safety and design invariants

- No background clipboard monitoring or automatic clipboard reads.
- Never log clipboard contents, OAuth tokens, API keys, or credentials.
- No silent administrator elevation, UAC bypass, ACL/ownership/file-permission changes.
- Read-only inspection by default; preview changes before applying them.
- File moves, writes, settings changes, process termination, and GUI interaction use the existing permission model.
- Prefer native PowerShell/.NET/Win32 and UI Automation; use CMD/VBScript only for a demonstrated compatibility requirement.
- Skills are guidance, not permission grants. Every action still passes through the same execution and confirmation path.
- Do not claim Windows runtime validation until tested on Windows.

Status: standalone headless entry points, user-authored skill loading, direct Win32 clipboard/window helpers, UI Automation inspection/actions, and local Windows commands are implemented on `work`. Windows runtime/parser validation remains outstanding.


